FINAL ANSWER:
**Short version:** Troy Goode created `lib/index.js` and still owns most of it. Douglas Christopher Wilson is the second-largest surviving author. Plain `git blame` is misleading here because of a recent reformat commit.

**Why plain blame misleads.** `62628c0` (2026-04-12, Fiona Formatter, "reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes") rewrote 214 lines. Plain blame therefore credits her with 89.9% of the file. That commit only changed whitespace and quotes. I re-ran `git blame -w` and ignored that commit. I also ignored `b2005d9` in the first run, which made no real difference to the numbers. The counts below are lines of the 238-line file at HEAD.

**Whose code is still in it (formatting commit ignored):**

| Author | Lines | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | ~157–159 (~66%) | Creator and maintainer |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | Vary-header handling, options-delegate fix, lint and build changes |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (and alex94puchades) | 12 + 4 | RegExp and array support for `options.origin`, 2015 |
| Raymond Feng | 7–9 | `applyHeaders` optimization, 2015 |
| max.laverse | 6 | Passing the preflight request on to `next()`, 2015 |
| LuisEGR | 6 | Unused-parameter lint cleanup, 2021 |
| Simon Mansfield, Igor Soarez, Benjamin Eidelman | 3 each | Origin checks, Vary on specific origins, Safari preflight workaround |
| 10 others | 1–2 each | Saad Tazi, Mathias Buus, Eric di Domenico, Alberto Leal, Tom Arad, Shane Tomlinson, Hannah Wolfe, Eran Tiktin, Chima Alaebo |

**How it developed (62 commits touched the file):**
- **2013 (Troy Goode):** The first commit on 2013-01-30 added 78 lines. Troy added case-insensitive header lookup, `origin: false` to disable CORS, request pause and resume for async middleware, and `use strict`. The big "wrapping up" rewrite on 2013-10-09 added origin callbacks (from Eric di Domenico) and non-Express and Connect support (Mathias Buus, then Troy).
- **2014:** Troy added `Access-Control-Expose-Headers` and Express 4 support. Contributors added PATCH as a default method, method-name normalization, and a fix so `options.origin` callbacks aren't overridden. Igor Soarez added `Vary: Origin`, and Troy switched it to the `vary` module.
- **2015:** Contributors added regexp and array `origin` matching, preflight pass-through to `next()`, and exposed headers on OPTIONS. Troy moved the file from JSLint to ESLint.
- **2016–2018:** Douglas Christopher Wilson took over most of the work, mainly Vary-header fixes, the options-delegate fix, and lint and build upgrades. The rest are small fixes from various contributors, such as Safari preflight, frozen options, and `maxAge: 0`.
- **2021 and later:** There is only one lint cleanup (LuisEGR, 2021). Then comes `b2005d9` (Troy, 2026-04-10, "annotate handlers"), which rewrote 12 lines. After that comes the whitespace and quote reformat.

**Caveats.**
- `-w` ignores whitespace only. The 4-space and double-quote reformat may have changed quoting on some lines. Lines whose quotes changed can still be credited to Fiona. That would explain why the two runs differ by a few lines (for example Troy's 157 and 159).
- Lines Troy rewrote in `b2005d9` may now be attributed to the earlier author. The first run ignored both commits, so those lines can be attributed to older authors.
- Blame shows who last touched a line. It does not show who designed the logic.
